      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When the last pallet arrives at the Patna warehouse, the final delivery and uncrating protocol begins immediately. The first checkpoint is a daylight verification against the original inventory bilty to confirm that every item listed in the shipment manifest is present, correctly labeled, and in its expected condition.</p>
<p>This step is performed by the receiving supervisor in the presence of the shipping clerk and the customer’s designated representative. If any discrepancy is found, it is logged and an investigation is launched before the item is accepted into the inventory system.</p>

<p>Once the bilty check is cleared, the focus shifts to the testing of all electrical and mechanical components. A qualified technician performs a quick functional test on each unit – for example, turning on appliances, checking motors, and verifying that all safety switches operate correctly.</p>
<p>Any unit that fails the test is immediately quarantined, repaired, or returned to the supplier, depending on the warranty terms. Documentation of the test results is attached to the item’s barcode record in the warehouse management system.</p>

<p>Following the testing phase, the uncrating team proceeds to cleanly place each piece of furniture into its designated location. The team follows the floor plan and the customer’s layout instructions, ensuring that each item is positioned on a clean, level surface.</p>
<p>Furniture is oriented according to the original packing diagram to preserve its aesthetic and functional alignment. The team also removes protective coverings, ensuring that no dust or debris remains on the finished surface.</p>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Finally, the packing debris removal is executed with speed and efficiency.</p>
